/-! # WalkingDouble/DoubleTileSeed — the free strict double category on the walking square: signature, the (width, height) tile folds, and the tile-pasting relation

The presentation of the **free strict double category on the walking square** as a signature.  There is ONE
object `star`, ONE horizontal 1-cell generator `hGen : star →ₕ star`, ONE vertical 1-cell generator
`vGen : star →ᵥ star`, and ONE generating square `alpha` whose four boundaries are the generators (top = bottom =
`hGen`, left = right = `vGen` — a `(1,1)`-endo square).  Squares are freely generated by `alpha`, closed under
horizontal composition (side-by-side, sharing a vertical boundary), vertical composition (stacked, sharing a
horizontal boundary), and horizontal / vertical identity squares, modulo the double-category coherences:

* **horizontal associativity** `hcomp (hcomp a b) c ≈ hcomp a (hcomp b c)`;
* **vertical associativity** `vcomp (vcomp a b) c ≈ vcomp a (vcomp b c)`;
* the **interchange law** `vcomp (hcomp a b) (hcomp c d) ≈ hcomp (vcomp a c) (vcomp b d)` — the one genuinely
  two-dimensional coherence, the algebraic content of a double category;
* the **horizontal / vertical unit laws** for the identity squares (guarded — see below).

## ★ Why a NEW carrier — a double category is not a category-over-a-graph

Unlike the 1-cell walkers (`WalkingBraid`, `WalkingCyclicThree`), which instantiate `ModeSignature` /
`ModalityPath` (the free CATEGORY on a graph), a double category has a genuinely 2-dimensional cell — a SQUARE
with FOUR boundaries composing in TWO directions.  No `ModalityPath` (linear composable words in one direction)
represents a square.  So brick 1 introduces a fresh inductive `DoubleTile` carrier and does NOT instantiate
`ModeSignature`.  This is the 2-D transpose of `WalkingOperad`'s `OperadTree`: there a single `Nat` (arity) reads
the boundary; here the PAIR `(tileWidth, tileHeight)` reads the double-cell boundary shape.

## ★ Why the carrier is UN-INDEXED (not `Tile : Nat → Nat → Type`)

If the carrier were `(width, height)`-indexed, the associativity relation would be HETEROGENEOUS — LHS index
`(a+b)+c`, RHS `a+(b+c)`, not definitionally equal — forcing a transport along `Nat.add_assoc` (a propext-leak
hazard and a proof headache; the same transport lives at the double-cat unit laws).  Un-indexed carrier ⟹ the
convertibility `DoubleTileConv` is HOMOGENEOUS ⟹ `tileWidth` / `tileHeight` are genuine `Nat` structural folds,
not type indices.  This is exactly the `OperadTreeSeed` un-indexed lesson, doubled.

## ★ Why the folds live HERE (before the relation)

The two identity-square unit laws are the one place where the double-cat dimension is genuinely load-bearing: a
single fixed `hUnit` (a horizontal identity of height 1) is a horizontal unit only for a HEIGHT-1 partner.  We
express that honestly as a `Nat`-equation GUARD on the fold (`tileHeight a = 1`), NOT as a carrier index — so the
carrier stays un-indexed and the guard carries no transport.  Because the guards mention `tileWidth` / `tileHeight`,
the folds must be defined BEFORE `DoubleTileConv`.  The SOUNDNESS theorems (`tileWidth_congr_of_conv`,
`tileHeight_congr_of_conv`) and non-vacuity live in the companion `DoubleTileDimension`.

## Scope — BRICK 1

This file ships the SIGNATURE (the walking-square orientation record + the generating tiles), the `(width, height)`
invariant folds with their definitional smokes, the sample tiles, the tile-pasting convertibility
`DoubleTileConv`, and the law-fire witnesses (interchange on the 2×2 grid, h/v associativity, guarded units).  The
SOUNDNESS (`convertible ⟹ equal (width, height)`) and non-vacuity separations live in `DoubleTileDimension`.  The
FULL word-problem DECISION (the `m×n`-grid normal form) is WP-DOUBLE BRICK 2 — NOT attempted here.

Raw Lean 4 + Init; the convertibility is an inductive `Prop`; per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` gated in the
audit twin.  Free of `propext`, `Quot.sound`, `Classical`, `sorry`, `native_decide`, `omega`. -/

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph

/-! ## The tile carrier -/

/-- ★ The **tile carrier** of the walking-square double category: an UN-INDEXED double-cell over the single
generating square.  `square` is the generating `(1,1)`-endo square `alpha`; `hUnit` is the horizontal-identity
square (width 0, height 1); `vUnit` is the vertical-identity square (width 1, height 0); `hcomp` pastes two tiles
side by side (horizontal composition, sharing a vertical boundary); `vcomp` stacks two tiles (vertical
composition, sharing a horizontal boundary).  A closed well-formed tile of shape `(m, n)` is the `m×n` grid — a
square `hGen^m ⇒ hGen^m` over `vGen^n`.  `hcomp` / `vcomp` are total (they represent the partial double-cat
compositions as a superset; the folds read only the boundary shape, and `DoubleTileConv` / soundness handle the
rest — standard for a soundness brick). -/
inductive DoubleTile where
  /-- The generating square `alpha` — a `(1,1)`-endo square (width 1, height 1). -/
  | square
  /-- The horizontal-identity square (width 0, height 1). -/
  | hUnit
  /-- The vertical-identity square (width 1, height 0). -/
  | vUnit
  /-- Horizontal pasting — two tiles side by side, sharing a vertical boundary. -/
  | hcomp : DoubleTile → DoubleTile → DoubleTile
  /-- Vertical pasting — two tiles stacked, sharing a horizontal boundary. -/
  | vcomp : DoubleTile → DoubleTile → DoubleTile

/-! ## The generating cells and their dimensions -/

/-- The three generating cells of the walking-square double category: the horizontal 1-cell `hGen`, the vertical
1-cell `vGen`, and the square generator `alpha`. -/
inductive DoubleGenerator where
  /-- The horizontal 1-cell generator `hGen`. -/
  | hGen
  /-- The vertical 1-cell generator `vGen`. -/
  | vGen
  /-- The generating square `alpha` (the 2-dimensional cell). -/
  | alpha

/-- The **cell dimension** of each generator: `hGen ↦ 1`, `vGen ↦ 1` (both 1-cells), `alpha ↦ 2` (the square).  A
full-enumeration structural fold (no wildcard), propext-clean. -/
def generatorDimension : DoubleGenerator → Nat
  | .hGen => 1
  | .vGen => 1
  | .alpha => 2

/-- Smoke: the horizontal 1-cell generator has dimension 1. -/
theorem generatorDimension_hGen : generatorDimension DoubleGenerator.hGen = 1 := rfl

/-- Smoke: the vertical 1-cell generator has dimension 1. -/
theorem generatorDimension_vGen : generatorDimension DoubleGenerator.vGen = 1 := rfl

/-- Smoke: the square generator `alpha` has dimension 2. -/
theorem generatorDimension_alpha : generatorDimension DoubleGenerator.alpha = 2 := rfl

/-! ## The walking-square orientation signature (cosmetic, not load-bearing)

The signature of the fixed double category, recording the boundary shape of the generating square `alpha`: it is a
`(1,1)`-endo square, so all four boundaries have extent 1 (top = bottom = `hGen`, one horizontal step each; left =
right = `vGen`, one vertical step each).  This is the ORIENTATION-only view mirroring `monoidOperadSignature`;
brick 1 does NOT build the generic free double category from an arbitrary such signature — that (many square
generators of the same shape) is a later, generator-generic brick. -/

/-- The **walking-square signature**: the four boundary extents of the generating square `alpha`. -/
structure WalkingSquareSignature where
  /-- The extent of the top horizontal boundary (in `hGen` steps). -/
  topBoundaryWidth : Nat
  /-- The extent of the bottom horizontal boundary (in `hGen` steps). -/
  bottomBoundaryWidth : Nat
  /-- The extent of the left vertical boundary (in `vGen` steps). -/
  leftBoundaryHeight : Nat
  /-- The extent of the right vertical boundary (in `vGen` steps). -/
  rightBoundaryHeight : Nat

/-- ★ The **walking-square signature value**: `alpha` is the `(1,1)`-endo square, so every boundary extent is 1. -/
def walkingSquareSignature : WalkingSquareSignature :=
  { topBoundaryWidth := 1, bottomBoundaryWidth := 1,
    leftBoundaryHeight := 1, rightBoundaryHeight := 1 }

/-- Smoke: the top horizontal boundary of `alpha` has extent 1 (`hGen`). -/
theorem walkingSquareSignature_topBoundaryWidth :
    walkingSquareSignature.topBoundaryWidth = 1 := rfl

/-- Smoke: the left vertical boundary of `alpha` has extent 1 (`vGen`). -/
theorem walkingSquareSignature_leftBoundaryHeight :
    walkingSquareSignature.leftBoundaryHeight = 1 := rfl

/-- Smoke: `alpha` is an ENDO square in the horizontal direction — top boundary equals bottom boundary. -/
theorem walkingSquareSignature_horizontalEndo :
    walkingSquareSignature.topBoundaryWidth = walkingSquareSignature.bottomBoundaryWidth := rfl

/-- Smoke: `alpha` is an ENDO square in the vertical direction — left boundary equals right boundary. -/
theorem walkingSquareSignature_verticalEndo :
    walkingSquareSignature.leftBoundaryHeight = walkingSquareSignature.rightBoundaryHeight := rfl

/-! ## The `(width, height)` invariant folds

The tile-pasting soundness invariant is the PAIR of `Nat` structural folds `(tileWidth, tileHeight)`, reading the
double-cell boundary shape.  Both are DATA-valued `casesOn` folds (full-enumeration, no index refinement), so the
defining equations reduce DEFINITIONALLY — exactly `OperadTree`'s `arityOf`, doubled.

`tileWidth`: `square ↦ 1`, `hUnit ↦ 0`, `vUnit ↦ 1`; `hcomp` (shared vertical extent) SUMS the widths; `vcomp`
(shared horizontal extent) reads the LEFT width.  `tileHeight` is the transpose: `hcomp` reads the LEFT height,
`vcomp` SUMS the heights.  Why the PAIR and not a single square-count: a count gives both `hcomp square square` and
`vcomp square square` the value 2 and CANNOT separate a `2×1` grid from a `1×2` grid; `(width, height)` separates
them `(2,1)` vs `(1,2)` — strictly richer, and directly the double-cat boundary. -/

/-- ★ The **width fold** — the horizontal extent of a tile.  `square ↦ 1`, `hUnit ↦ 0`, `vUnit ↦ 1`; a horizontal
paste `hcomp` sums the children's widths; a vertical paste `vcomp` reads the (shared) left width. -/
def tileWidth : DoubleTile → Nat
  | .square => 1
  | .hUnit => 0
  | .vUnit => 1
  | .hcomp a b => tileWidth a + tileWidth b
  | .vcomp a _ => tileWidth a

/-- ★ The **height fold** — the vertical extent of a tile.  `square ↦ 1`, `hUnit ↦ 1`, `vUnit ↦ 0`; a horizontal
paste `hcomp` reads the (shared) left height; a vertical paste `vcomp` sums the children's heights. -/
def tileHeight : DoubleTile → Nat
  | .square => 1
  | .hUnit => 1
  | .vUnit => 0
  | .hcomp a _ => tileHeight a
  | .vcomp a b => tileHeight a + tileHeight b

/-- The width defining equation on `square` — the generating square has width 1. -/
theorem tileWidth_square : tileWidth DoubleTile.square = 1 := rfl

/-- The width defining equation on `hUnit` — the horizontal-identity square has width 0. -/
theorem tileWidth_hUnit : tileWidth DoubleTile.hUnit = 0 := rfl

/-- The width defining equation on `vUnit` — the vertical-identity square has width 1. -/
theorem tileWidth_vUnit : tileWidth DoubleTile.vUnit = 1 := rfl

/-- The width defining equation on `hcomp` — horizontal pasting SUMS the widths.  Holds DEFINITIONALLY. -/
theorem tileWidth_hcomp (a b : DoubleTile) :
    tileWidth (DoubleTile.hcomp a b) = tileWidth a + tileWidth b := rfl

/-- The width defining equation on `vcomp` — vertical pasting reads the (shared) left width.  Holds
DEFINITIONALLY. -/
theorem tileWidth_vcomp (a b : DoubleTile) :
    tileWidth (DoubleTile.vcomp a b) = tileWidth a := rfl

/-- The height defining equation on `square` — the generating square has height 1. -/
theorem tileHeight_square : tileHeight DoubleTile.square = 1 := rfl

/-- The height defining equation on `hUnit` — the horizontal-identity square has height 1. -/
theorem tileHeight_hUnit : tileHeight DoubleTile.hUnit = 1 := rfl

/-- The height defining equation on `vUnit` — the vertical-identity square has height 0. -/
theorem tileHeight_vUnit : tileHeight DoubleTile.vUnit = 0 := rfl

/-- The height defining equation on `hcomp` — horizontal pasting reads the (shared) left height.  Holds
DEFINITIONALLY. -/
theorem tileHeight_hcomp (a b : DoubleTile) :
    tileHeight (DoubleTile.hcomp a b) = tileHeight a := rfl

/-- The height defining equation on `vcomp` — vertical pasting SUMS the heights.  Holds DEFINITIONALLY. -/
theorem tileHeight_vcomp (a b : DoubleTile) :
    tileHeight (DoubleTile.vcomp a b) = tileHeight a + tileHeight b := rfl

/-! ## Concrete sample tiles -/

/-- ★ The interchange law's left-hand tile — the 2×2 grid built vertical-of-horizontals:
`vcomp (hcomp square square) (hcomp square square)`.  Shape `(2, 2)`. -/
def doubleGridInterchangeLeft : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.vcomp (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)
    (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)

/-- ★ The interchange law's right-hand tile — the SAME 2×2 grid built horizontal-of-verticals:
`hcomp (vcomp square square) (vcomp square square)`.  Shape `(2, 2)`. -/
def doubleGridInterchangeRight : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.hcomp (DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)
    (DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)

/-- The horizontal-associativity law's left-hand tile `hcomp (hcomp square square) square` — a left-nested
horizontal paste of three squares.  Shape `(3, 1)`. -/
def doubleHAssocLeft : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.hcomp (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square) DoubleTile.square

/-- The horizontal-associativity law's right-hand tile `hcomp square (hcomp square square)` — the right-nested
horizontal paste of the same three squares.  Shape `(3, 1)`. -/
def doubleHAssocRight : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)

/-- The vertical-associativity law's left-hand tile `vcomp (vcomp square square) square` — a left-nested vertical
paste of three squares.  Shape `(1, 3)`. -/
def doubleVAssocLeft : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.vcomp (DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square) DoubleTile.square

/-- The vertical-associativity law's right-hand tile `vcomp square (vcomp square square)` — the right-nested
vertical paste of the same three squares.  Shape `(1, 3)`. -/
def doubleVAssocRight : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.square (DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square)

/-- The horizontal-left-unit law's left-hand tile `hcomp hUnit square` — the horizontal identity pasted on the
left of a height-1 square.  Shape `(1, 1)`. -/
def doubleHUnitLeftTile : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.hUnit DoubleTile.square

/-- The vertical-left-unit law's left-hand tile `vcomp vUnit square` — the vertical identity pasted on top of a
width-1 square.  Shape `(1, 1)`. -/
def doubleVUnitLeftTile : DoubleTile :=
  DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.vUnit DoubleTile.square

/-! ## The tile-pasting convertibility -/

/-- ★ The **tile-pasting convertibility** of the walking-square double category — the free double-category
convertibility closed under the interchange law, horizontal / vertical associativity, the guarded horizontal /
vertical unit laws, the two directional congruences (reaching into both children of a paste), and
`refl` / `symm` / `trans`.  Two tiles denote the same double-cell exactly when they are `DoubleTileConv`-related.

Interchange and the two associativities are UNGUARDED — their soundness holds for ARBITRARY tiles (interchange
preserves both `tileWidth` and `tileHeight` DEFINITIONALLY; associativity preserves the adding dimension by
`Nat.add_assoc` and the other by `rfl`).  The unit laws are GUARDED by a plain `Nat` equation on the fold (NOT by
carrier indexing): a single fixed `hUnit` (height 1) is a horizontal unit only for a height-1 partner, and the
guard `tileHeight a = 1` is exactly the honest, transport-free treatment of that one dimension-sensitive pasting.
The `hcompCongr` / `vcompCongr` generators are the 2-D analog of `OperadTree`'s `mulCongr`; with the root-firing
laws + `symm` / `trans` they generate the full double-category congruence. -/
inductive DoubleTileConv : DoubleTile → DoubleTile → Prop where
  /-- **Interchange** `vcomp (hcomp a b) (hcomp c d) ≈ hcomp (vcomp a c) (vcomp b d)` — the genuinely
  two-dimensional coherence: pasting four tiles as a `2×2` block is order-independent. -/
  | interchange (a b c d : DoubleTile) :
      DoubleTileConv
        (DoubleTile.vcomp (DoubleTile.hcomp a b) (DoubleTile.hcomp c d))
        (DoubleTile.hcomp (DoubleTile.vcomp a c) (DoubleTile.vcomp b d))
  /-- **Horizontal associativity** `hcomp (hcomp a b) c ≈ hcomp a (hcomp b c)`. -/
  | hAssoc (a b c : DoubleTile) :
      DoubleTileConv
        (DoubleTile.hcomp (DoubleTile.hcomp a b) c)
        (DoubleTile.hcomp a (DoubleTile.hcomp b c))
  /-- **Vertical associativity** `vcomp (vcomp a b) c ≈ vcomp a (vcomp b c)`. -/
  | vAssoc (a b c : DoubleTile) :
      DoubleTileConv
        (DoubleTile.vcomp (DoubleTile.vcomp a b) c)
        (DoubleTile.vcomp a (DoubleTile.vcomp b c))
  /-- **Horizontal left unit** `hcomp hUnit a ≈ a`, guarded by `tileHeight a = 1` (the horizontal identity is a
  left unit only for a height-1 partner).  The guard is a `Nat` equation, NOT a carrier index. -/
  | hUnitLeft (a : DoubleTile) (guard : tileHeight a = 1) :
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.hUnit a) a
  /-- **Horizontal right unit** `hcomp a hUnit ≈ a`, guarded by `tileHeight a = 1`. -/
  | hUnitRight (a : DoubleTile) (guard : tileHeight a = 1) :
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.hcomp a DoubleTile.hUnit) a
  /-- **Vertical left unit** `vcomp vUnit a ≈ a`, guarded by `tileWidth a = 1` (the vertical identity is a left
  unit only for a width-1 partner). -/
  | vUnitLeft (a : DoubleTile) (guard : tileWidth a = 1) :
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.vcomp DoubleTile.vUnit a) a
  /-- **Vertical right unit** `vcomp a vUnit ≈ a`, guarded by `tileWidth a = 1`. -/
  | vUnitRight (a : DoubleTile) (guard : tileWidth a = 1) :
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.vcomp a DoubleTile.vUnit) a
  /-- **Congruence under horizontal pasting** — reaching into BOTH children: `aOld ≈ aNew` and `bOld ≈ bNew` give
  `hcomp aOld bOld ≈ hcomp aNew bNew`. -/
  | hcompCongr {aOld aNew bOld bNew : DoubleTile} :
      DoubleTileConv aOld aNew → DoubleTileConv bOld bNew →
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.hcomp aOld bOld) (DoubleTile.hcomp aNew bNew)
  /-- **Congruence under vertical pasting** — reaching into BOTH children: `aOld ≈ aNew` and `bOld ≈ bNew` give
  `vcomp aOld bOld ≈ vcomp aNew bNew`. -/
  | vcompCongr {aOld aNew bOld bNew : DoubleTile} :
      DoubleTileConv aOld aNew → DoubleTileConv bOld bNew →
      DoubleTileConv (DoubleTile.vcomp aOld bOld) (DoubleTile.vcomp aNew bNew)
  /-- Reflexivity. -/
  | refl (tile : DoubleTile) : DoubleTileConv tile tile
  /-- Symmetry. -/
  | symm {tile1 tile2 : DoubleTile} : DoubleTileConv tile1 tile2 → DoubleTileConv tile2 tile1
  /-- Transitivity. -/
  | trans {tile1 tile2 tile3 : DoubleTile} :
      DoubleTileConv tile1 tile2 → DoubleTileConv tile2 tile3 → DoubleTileConv tile1 tile3

/-- ★ **Interchange holds** — the star witness: the 2×2 grid `vcomp (hcomp square square) (hcomp square square)`
is convertible to `hcomp (vcomp square square) (vcomp square square)` (both are the literal picture of
interchange, both of shape `(2, 2)`). -/
theorem doubleGridInterchangeHolds :
    DoubleTileConv doubleGridInterchangeLeft doubleGridInterchangeRight :=
  DoubleTileConv.interchange DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square

/-- ★ **Horizontal associativity holds** — `hcomp (hcomp square square) square ≈ hcomp square (hcomp square square)`
(at three squares). -/
theorem doubleHAssocHolds :
    DoubleTileConv doubleHAssocLeft doubleHAssocRight :=
  DoubleTileConv.hAssoc DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square

/-- ★ **Vertical associativity holds** — `vcomp (vcomp square square) square ≈ vcomp square (vcomp square square)`
(at three squares). -/
theorem doubleVAssocHolds :
    DoubleTileConv doubleVAssocLeft doubleVAssocRight :=
  DoubleTileConv.vAssoc DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square

/-- ★ **Horizontal left unit holds** — `hcomp hUnit square ≈ square`: a GENUINE guarded-law firing, its guard
`tileHeight square = 1` discharged by `rfl`. -/
theorem doubleHUnitLeftHolds :
    DoubleTileConv doubleHUnitLeftTile DoubleTile.square :=
  DoubleTileConv.hUnitLeft DoubleTile.square rfl

/-- ★ **Vertical left unit holds** — `vcomp vUnit square ≈ square`: a GENUINE guarded-law firing, its guard
`tileWidth square = 1` discharged by `rfl`. -/
theorem doubleVUnitLeftHolds :
    DoubleTileConv doubleVUnitLeftTile DoubleTile.square :=
  DoubleTileConv.vUnitLeft DoubleTile.square rfl

/-- Smoke: the horizontal-left-unit law fires WHISKERED under a horizontal paste —
`hcomp (hcomp hUnit square) square ≈ hcomp square square` — exercising `hcompCongr` (left child rewritten by the
unit law, right child by `refl`). -/
theorem doubleHUnitLeftWhiskeredHolds :
    DoubleTileConv
      (DoubleTile.hcomp doubleHUnitLeftTile DoubleTile.square)
      (DoubleTile.hcomp DoubleTile.square DoubleTile.square) :=
  DoubleTileConv.hcompCongr doubleHUnitLeftHolds (DoubleTileConv.refl DoubleTile.square)

end FX1Poly.Polygraph
